    <sys:String x:Key="S_SecurityNotes">Security notes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S_SecurityNotesHint">Read this before handing the client to a customer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S_SecNotePrivateKey">The private key file is encrypted with AES-256 (PBKDF2, 600 000 iterations). Back it up separately from the password, and never ship it with the licensed application.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S_SecNoteDpapi">The client stores the license with DPAPI and additional entropy derived from the machine fingerprint. The clock state is protected the same way, so moving the license file or the clock state to another PC fails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S_SecNoteOffline">A fully offline application cannot reliably enforce revocation or resist clock tampering if the local state is deleted. Keep this model for convenience and add periodic server validation when the commercial value justifies it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S_SecNoteObfuscation">Use obfuscation and code signing for release builds. They raise the cost of tampering but do not replace cryptographic verification.</sys:String>

